From 886b64ffc6983f8fc8f53291000176c7365d0909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): lane slots never leak and stay held until the
 thread returns [daveey]

Review of #3936:
- _admit: a cancellation landing right after the gate handed the slot over
  left it held forever (two /api/status active-count timeouts filled the probe
  lane). Acquisition is now recorded as soon as acquire returns, and any
  exception releases a slot already taken. The disconnect poll never
  overrides an acquisition.
- run_in_lane: a caller cancelled while its thread ran (e.g. /api/status's
  0.75 s wait_for) freed the slot while the read kept running, so a lane did
  not bound its threads. The slot and counters are now released by the
  thread when it returns; work cancelled before a thread picked it up never
  starts.
- New kanban lane (4) for /api/session-kanban-tasks: polled per sidebar row
  and slow when a board is busy, it no longer shares the session lists'
  threads.
- configure() swaps the lane table in one assignment.
- Docs: request= only where the body is already read; coalesced callers wait
  on coalesced_read's own admission first.

Tests: a cancel 0-5 loop turns after the hand-off leaves nothing borrowed
(failed on the previous head); a caller cancelled mid-run keeps its slot
until the thread returns (failed on the previous head); an exception from the
work releases the slot; a disconnect racing the hand-off leaves nothing
borrowed (guards the invariant; the old leak depended on task order and did
not reproduce here). The load test now also requires the slow kanban reads to
leave the sessions lane empty.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
